From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 01:01:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: extend offloaded GRE conntrack timeouts
 from the GC

The flowtable GC re-extends every offloaded conntrack it keeps
(nf_flow_table_extend_ct_timeout(), 03428ca5cee9 and 53b3e60edb67), but
knows only TCP and UDP. nft_flow_offload_eval() admits GRE too, and a GRE
flow lands in the switch's default: a WARN, and a new timeout of one
jiffy, so its conntrack expires within a pass and the GC then retires the
live hardware flow as dying. Extend GRE as UDP is, to a day.

The comment patch 142 left in flow_offload_teardown() names this refresher
instead of gc_worker.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
index 15de5b49f5d90..fa43f37fc89a3 100644
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
@@ -556,9 +556,9 @@ void flow_offload_teardown(struct flow_offload *flow)
 	 * cleanup sweep over its device calls this again while the flow waits
 	 * for its hardware retirement, and a tuple reopened in the meantime has
 	 * already given the conntrack to a new flow, which the repeat would rob
-	 * of the only refresh it can get: gc_worker skips conntracks without
-	 * IPS_OFFLOAD, and the new flow is forwarded in hardware, so no packet
-	 * reaches the software path to set the bit again.
+	 * of the only refresh it can get: nf_flow_table_extend_ct_timeout()
+	 * skips conntracks without IPS_OFFLOAD, and the new flow is forwarded in
+	 * hardware, so no packet reaches the software path to set the bit again.
 	 */
 	if (!test_and_set_bit(NF_FLOW_TEARDOWN, &flow->flags)) {
 		clear_bit(IPS_OFFLOAD_BIT, &flow->ct->status);
@@ -707,6 +707,10 @@ static void nf_flow_table_extend_ct_timeout(struct nf_conn *ct)
 
 		switch (l4proto) {
 		case IPPROTO_UDP:
+		/* The flowtable admits GRE (nft_flow_offload_eval()), and
+		 * extends it as it does UDP.
+		 */
+		case IPPROTO_GRE:
 			new_timeout = NF_CT_DAY;
 			break;
 		case IPPROTO_TCP:
